2025-06-01 20:47:58,001 - multi_agent_system.agent.11 - INFO - [execute_with_tools] Starting execution with command: {"task_description": "Write a hello world pyspark code", "requirements": {"min_accuracy": 0.85, "max_time": 1800, "specific_tools": ["pyspark"], "output_format": "python_code", "code_requirements": {"must_include": ["SparkSession", "create simple RDD", "basic transformation", "show output"], "style_guide": "PEP 8", "comments_required": true}}, "conversation_context": [{"agent_id": 10, "response": "Here is a simple example of a \"Hello, World!\" PySpark script. This script uses the SparkSession, creates a simple RDD, performs a basic transformation, and shows the output.\n\n```python\n# Import SparkSession from pyspark.sql\nfrom pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n\n# Create a SparkSession\nspark = SparkSession.builder.appName('HelloWorldApp').getOrCreate()\n\n# Create a simple RDD\ndata = ['Hello', 'World']\nrdd = spark.sparkContext.parallelize(data)\n\n# Perform a basic transformation using map() function\nrdd = rdd.map(lambda word: (word, 1))\n\n# Collect the results and print\nfor word in rdd.collect():\n    print(word)\n\n# Stop the SparkSession\nspark.stop()\n```\nThis script adheres to the PEP 8 style guide and includes comments explaining what each part of the code does. The SparkSession is created using the SparkSession.builder method. The appName('HelloWorldApp') method names the Spark application, which can be useful when running multiple Spark applications. The getOrCreate() method gets the existing SparkSession or, if there is no existing one, creates a new one. The parallelize method is used to create an RDD from the data list. The map() function applies a lambda function to each element of the RDD. The lambda function takes a word and returns a tuple containing the word and the number 1. The collect() method is used to retrieve all the elements of the RDD as an array to the driver program, which are then printed. The SparkSession is stopped at the end of the program."}], "accuracy_threshold": 0.8, "success_rate": 0.9}
