arkSession\n  .builder()\n  .appName(\"JDBC to DB2\")\n  .getOrCreate()\n\nval connectionProperties = new Properties()\nconnectionProperties.put(\"user\", \"your-username\")\nconnectionProperties.put(\"password\", \"your-password\")\n\nval jdbcDF = spark.read\n  .jdbc(\"jdbc:postgresql:dbserver\", \"database-name\", connectionProperties)\n\njdbcDF.show()\n\n```\n\nPlease replace `\"your-username\"` and `\"your-password\"` with your actual username and password for the database server. Also replace `\"jdbc:postgresql:dbserver\"` with your JDBC URL and `\"database-name\"` with the name of your database.\n\nIf this code runs without throwing any exceptions and displays some data from your database, then your connection is successful.\n\nPlease note that you need to have the correct JDBC driver in your classpath to connect to your specific type of database server.\n\nFor more complex scenarios (like connection pools, dealing with connection loss etc.) you might want to use a database connection library that is compatible with Spark."}], "accuracy_threshold": 0.8, "success_rate": 0.9}
